[
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "We are deeply grieved at thy delay in strengthening us by thy addresses and consolations.",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If thy absence be prolonged, it will disappoint many of us. Hasten then to come, for we believe that it is expedient.",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "There are also many of our women here, who are desirous to see Mary [the mother] of Jesus, and wish day by day to run off from us to you,",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "that they may meet with her, and touch those breasts of hers which nourished the Lord Jesus, and may inquire of her respecting some rather secret matters.",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But Salome also, [the daughter of Anna,] whom thou lovest, who stayed with her five months at Jerusalem, and some other well-known persons,",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "relate that she is full of all graces and all virtues, after the manner of a virgin, fruitful in virtue and grace.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And, as they report, she is cheerful in persecutions and afflictions, free from murmuring in the midst of penury and want, grateful to those that injure her, and rejoices when exposed to troubles:",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "she sympathizes with the wretched and the afflicted as sharing in their afflictions, and is not slow to come to their assistance.",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Moreover, she shines forth gloriously as contending in the fight of faith against the pernicious conflicts of vicious principles or conduct.",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "She is the lady of our new religion and repentance, and the handmaid among the faithful of all works of piety.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "She is indeed devoted to the humble, and she humbles herself more devotedly than the devoted, and is wonderfully magnified by all, while at the same time she suffers detraction from the Scribes and Pharisees.",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s12",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Besides these points, many relate to us numerous other things regarding her. We do not, however, go so far as to believe all in every particular; nor do we mention such to thee.",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s13",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s13",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But, as we are informed by those who are worthy of credit, there is in Mary the mother of Jesus an angelic purity of nature allied with the nature of humanity.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s14",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s14",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And such reports as these have greatly excited our emotions, and urge us eagerly to desire a sight of this (if it be lawful so to speak) heavenly prodigy and most sacred marvel.",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s15",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn1.i.s15",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But do thou in haste comply with this our desire; and fare thou well. Amen.",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If thou wilt give me leave, I desire to go up to Jerusalem, and see the faithful saints who are there, especially Mary the mother, whom they report to be an object of admiration and of affection to all.",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For who would not rejoice to behold and to address her who bore the true God from her own womb, provided he is a friend of our faith and religion?",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And in like manner [I desire to see] the venerable James, who is surnamed Just, whom they relate to be very like Christ Jesus in appearance,",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "in life, and in method of conduct, as if he were a twin-brother of the same womb.",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "They say that, if I see him, I see also Jesus Himself, as to all the features and aspect of His body.",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Moreover, [I desire to see] the other saints, both male and female. Alas! why do I delay?",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Jn2.i.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Why am I kept back? Kind teacher, bid me hasten [to fulfil my wish], and fare thou well. Amen.",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Thou oughtest to have comforted and consoled me who am a neophyte, and a disciple of thy [beloved] John.",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For I have heard things wonderful to tell respecting thy [son] Jesus, and I am astonished by such a report.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But I desire with my whole heart to obtain information concerning the things which I have heard from thee, who wast always intimate and allied with Him, and who wast acquainted with [all] His secrets.",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I have also written to thee at another time, and have asked thee concerning the same things.",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.Mar.i.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Fare thou well; and let the neophytes who are with me be comforted of thee, and by thee, and in thee. Amen.",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.MarIgn.i.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.MarIgn.i.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The things which thou hast heard and learned from John concerning Jesus are true. Believe them, cling to them, and hold fast the profession of that Christianity which thou hast embraced, and conform thy habits and life to thy profession.",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.MarIgn.i.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.MarIgn.i.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Now I will come in company with John to visit thee, and those that are with thee.",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence#PsIgnLat.MarIgn.i.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/ignatius-latin-correspondence",
    "canonical_ref": "PsIgnLat.MarIgn.i.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Stand fast in the faith, and show thyself a man; nor let the fierceness of persecution move thee, but let thy spirit be strong and rejoice in God thy Saviour. Amen.",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": null,
    "date_range": [
      800,
      1150
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  }
]